{"step_index":1484,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:35:41Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-03T01:05:41+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-03T01:05:41+05:30\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\n<USER_REQUEST>\r\nCRITICAL PARSER REFACTOR: IMPLEMENT 3-TIER PRODUCTION INVOICE EXTRACTION PIPELINE\r\n\r\nRefactor our invoice parsing pipeline across backend and client fallback to eliminate brittle line-by-line regex. Implement these 3 steps:\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nSTEP 1: TABLE-ANCHOR BOUNDARY SLICING (in invoiceTextParser.js / parser logic)\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nStop running OCR regex top-to-bottom across the entire document text. Instead, slice the document into 3 distinct vertical zones:\r\n1. HEADER ZONE (Top to Table Start):\r\n   - Start: Beginning of text.\r\n   - End: Table Header row containing at least two keywords: ['Description', 'Item', 'Particulars', 'HSN', 'Qty', 'Rate', 'Amount'].\r\n   - Purpose: Extract Vendor Name, GSTIN, Invoice Number, and Date ONLY.\r\n   - Guardrail: Never extract any line from this zone as an item, even if it contains numbers, addresses ('Shop No', 'Plot', 'Bazaar'), or phone numbers.\r\n\r\n2. LINE ITEM ZONE (Strict Table Boundaries):\r\n   - Start: Immediately after the Table Header row.\r\n   - End: Table Footer row matching: ['Subtotal', 'Item Subtotal', 'Taxable Value', 'Total Tax', 'CGST', 'SGST', 'IGST', 'Total in Words'].\r\n   - Purpose: Extract ONLY physical products/services strictly located between these two boundaries. Discard any line without a valid product name and positive rate/amount.\r\n\r\n3. SUMMARY & TAX ZONE (Table End to Bottom):\r\n   - Start: Subtotal / Tax rows down to the end of the text.\r\n   - Purpose: Extract Subtotal, CGST, SGST, IGST, and the printed Grand Total ('Invoice Total Demanded', 'Net Payable', 'Grand Total').\r\n   - Guardrail: Bank details, payment notes, and terms & conditions belong here and must never leak into items.\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nSTEP 2: RIGHT-\n<truncated 215 bytes>\nThird-to-Last Number) = Quantity (quantity)\r\n   - Token 4 (Optional Number) = HSN/SAC code (4 to 8 digits)\r\n3. Everything remaining to the left of these numeric tokens = Description.\r\n4. Validation Check:\r\n   - Discard the line if (quantity * unit_rate) deviates by more than 5% from total_amount unless a known discount column exists.\r\n   - Strip leading/trailing punctuation and unit abbreviations ('NOS', 'PCS', '|', '[', ']').\r\n\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nSTEP 3: GEMINI VISION MULTIMODAL EXTRACTION AS PRIMARY (FastAPI / Backend)\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nEnsure client-side text parsing is strictly a fallback. Route the primary extraction through Gemini 2.5 Flash using direct visual layout understanding:\r\n\r\n1. Send the file bytes directly (image/jpeg, image/png, or application/pdf) using the Gemini 2.5 Flash model with temperature=0.0.\r\n2. Support both API key formats in headers:\r\n   - If key starts with 'AQ.': pass as Authorization: Bearer <key>\r\n   - Otherwise: pass as x-goog-api-key: <key>\r\n3. Use a structured JSON schema:\r\n   {\r\n     \"vendor_name\": string,\r\n     \"gstin\": string,\r\n     \"invoice_number\": string,\r\n     \"items\": [\r\n       {\"description\": string, \"quantity\": number, \"unit_rate\": number, \"total_amount\": number}\r\n     ],\r\n     \"subtotal\": number,\r\n     \"cgst\": number,\r\n     \"sgst\": number,\r\n     \"igst\": number,\r\n     \"declared_total\": number\r\n   }\r\n4. Post-processing reconciliation:\r\n   - Ensure declared_total matches the printed total on the bill. If declared_total is suspiciously less than 50% of subtotal (e.g., extracting an HSN/tax fragment like 774 or 20), recalculate declared_total = subtotal + cgst + sgst + igst.\r\n   - Synchronize property names: set both `declared_total` and `total_declared` to the same value so the frontend audit engine never receives undefined.\r\n</USER_REQUEST>\r\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\r\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-03T01:00:39+05:30.\r\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\r\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
